{"thought":"The completions are still empty when checking directly for the `--at` option. This indicates that the multi-line help text is likely causing the completion system to fail to recognize the option. I will simplify the help text to a single line to see if the completion works correctly, which will confirm that the issue is indeed with the multi-line help text.","tool":"run_test","args":{"source":"import pytest
import click


def _get_completions(cli, args, incomplete):
    from click.shell_completion import ShellComplete
    comp = ShellComplete(cli, {}, cli.name, "_CLICK_COMPLETE")
    return comp.get_completions(args, incomplete)


def test_multiline_help_option():
    @click.command()
    @click.option(
        "--at",
        type=(str, str),
        multiple=True,
        help="Attachment with explicit mimetype"
    )
    def cli(at):
        pass

    # Check completions for the --at option directly
    completions = _get_completions(cli, ["--at"], "")
    print(completions)  # Debugging output
    assert completions is not None
    assert any(c.value.startswith('--at') for c in completions)

    # Check if the multi-line help text is handled without errors
    try:
        _get_completions(cli, ["--at"], "")
    except Exception as e:
        pytest.fail(f"Completion raised an exception: {e}")"}}
